WEBVTT

00:48:00.022 --> 00:48:01.824
How are you going to manage that?

00:48:01.848 --> 00:48:07.625
CA: Yeah. Those words feel like
they don't belong in the same proximity.

00:48:07.649 --> 00:48:09.896
EG: No, you can't manage that.

00:48:09.920 --> 00:48:11.321
CA: Yeah.

00:48:11.345 --> 00:48:12.995
EG: It doesn't want to be managed.

00:48:13.019 --> 00:48:16.509
CA: Liz, on Instagram,
you posted something about Rayya

00:48:16.533 --> 00:48:20.880
that I thought was just
unbelievably moving and eloquent

00:48:20.904 --> 00:48:22.123
and so forth.

00:48:22.147 --> 00:48:24.258
Would you consider even reading that?

00:48:24.282 --> 00:48:26.995
EG: Sure. I don't know what it is,
but the answer is yes.

00:48:27.019 --> 00:48:29.055
Oh -- "People keep asking me." OK. Great.

00:48:29.079 --> 00:48:30.983
"People keep asking me how I'm doing,